Feature: Add greeting_has_comma library probe
  As a maintainer exercising nmg-sdlc against this disposable Python host
  I want a greeting_has_comma(name) library probe
  So that the complete default greeting can be checked for a literal comma without changing greet or the CLI

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Default Ada greeting reports the comma separator
    Given the library is importable
    When greeting_has_comma is called with Ada
    Then it returns the Python bool True
    And that value matches whether greet Ada contains the literal comma separator

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A second valid name is also true and is not hardcoded to Ada
    Given the library is importable
    When greeting_has_comma is called with Jo
    Then it returns the Python bool True
    And that value matches whether greet Jo contains the literal comma separator
    And greet Jo is not the same string as greet Ada

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Invalid names reuse existing validation
    Given the library is importable
    When greeting_has_comma is called with a blank, whitespace-only, or non-string name
    Then it raises ValueError with message name must not be blank
    And that error is the existing greet validation error, not a wrapped or renamed error

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Existing greet and CLI behavior is unchanged
    Given the distribution is installed
    When greet is called with Ada
    Then it returns Hello, Ada
    When nmg-smoke Ada is run
    Then the process exits 0 and prints Hello, Ada followed by a single newline
    And no new CLI flag or CLI output path is added
